# Cholecystectomy

- **Pre-operative preparation:**
  - Assessment of fitness for procedure - CBC, LRFT, Clotting profiles (liver synthetic function), CXR and ECG (if \> 45y or medically indicated)
  - Prophylactic ABx - 2nd generation cephalosporin
  - DVT prophylaxis (unsure if necessary in our locality) - subcutaneous heparin and anti-embolic stockings
  - Signed informed consent
- **Laprascopic cholecystectomy:**
  - Subumbilical port - establish pneumoperitoneum and insertion of telescope
  - 3 other operative ports - xiphisternum, and 2 in right costal area
- **Open cholecystectomy** - upper midline or short right upper transverse incision
- **Complications of cholecystectomy:**
  - Early complications - access complications, bile duct leakge
  - Late complications (post-cholecystectomy syndrome):
    - Post-cholecystectomy choledocholithiasis
    - Strictures of bile duct
    - Choledochotomy

